[agent:result] # Lakebase synced tables
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] > **Official docs:** https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/oltp/projects/sync-tables
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Lakebase synced tables sync data from Unity Catalog Delta tables into Lakebase as PostgreSQL tables for OLTP access patterns. Previously known as **Reverse ETL**.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] **How it works:** Synced tables create a managed copy — a Unity Catalog table (read-only, managed by sync pipeline) and a Postgres table in Lakebase (queryable by apps). Uses managed Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] **Performance (per Autoscaling CU):**
[agent:result] - Continuous/Triggered: ~150 rows/sec per CU
[agent:result] - Snapshot: ~2,000 rows/sec per CU
[agent:result] - Each synced table uses up to 16 connections
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ## Sync Modes
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] | Mode | Description | CDF Required | Best For |
[agent:result] |------|-------------|-------------|----------|
[agent:result] | **Snapshot** | One-time full copy | No | Initial setup, small tables, >10% data change |
[agent:result] | **Triggered** | Scheduled updates | Yes | Dashboards updated hourly/daily |
[agent:result] | **Continuous** | Real-time (seconds latency, 15s min interval) | Yes | Live applications |
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] **Enable CDF on source table:**
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ```sql
[agent:result] ALTER TABLE your_catalog.your_schema.your_table
[agent:result] SET TBLPROPERTIES (delta.enableChangeDataFeed = true)
[agent:result] ```
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ## Prerequisites
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] - A Databricks workspace with Lakebase enabled
[agent:result] - An active Lakebase project with a branch and endpoint
[agent:result] - A Unity Catalog source table to sync
[agent:result] - **Permissions:** `USE_SCHEMA` and `CREATE_TABLE` on the target schema
[agent:result] - For Triggered/Continuous modes: Change Data Feed enabled on the source table
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] > **Note:** Your Lakebase database must be registered as a UC catalog (one-time setup per project). Skip if already done.
[agent:result] >
[agent:result] > ```bash
[agent:result] > databricks postgres create-catalog <CATALOG_NAME> \
[agent:result] >   --json '{
[agent:result] >     "spec": {
[agent:result] >       "postgres_database": "<POSTGRES_DATABASE>",
[agent:result] >       "branch": "projects/<PROJECT_ID>/branches/<BRANCH_ID>"
[agent:result] >     }
[agent:result] >   }' --profile <PROFILE>
[agent:result] > ```
[agent:result] >
[agent:result] > The `<POSTGRES_DATABASE>` is the Postgres database name (default: `databricks_postgres`), not the resource path.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ## Creating Lakebase synced tables
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] > **Source table must exist first.** Synced tables sync from an existing UC table, view, or materialized view. If the source needs transformation, ask the user how they want to prepare it (DLT materialized view, regular view, or existing table). Do not run ad-hoc `CREATE TABLE AS SELECT` statements.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ```bash
[agent:result] databricks postgres create-synced-table <LAKEBASE_CATALOG>.<SCHEMA>.<TABLE> \
[agent:result]   --json '{
[agent:result]     "spec": {
[agent:result]       "source_table_full_name": "analytics.gold.user_profiles",
[agent:result]       "primary_key_columns": ["user_id"],
[agent:result]       "scheduling_policy": "TRIGGERED",
[agent:result]       "branch": "projects/<PROJECT_ID>/branches/production",
[agent:result]       "postgres_database": "databricks_postgres",
[agent:result]       "create_database_objects_if_missing": true,
[agent:result]       "new_pipeline_spec": {
[agent:result]         "storage_catalog": "<REGULAR_UC_CATALOG>",
[agent:result]         "storage_schema": "default"
[agent:result]       }
[agent:result]     }
[agent:result]   }' --profile <PROFILE>
[agent:result] ```
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] | Field | Required | Description |
[agent:result] |-------|----------|-------------|
[agent:result] | `source_table_full_name` | Yes | Full Unity Catalog name of the source table |
[agent:result] | `primary_key_columns` | Yes | Column(s) forming the primary key |
[agent:result] | `scheduling_policy` | Yes | `SNAPSHOT`, `TRIGGERED`, or `CONTINUOUS` |
[agent:result] | `branch` | Yes | Target Lakebase branch (`projects/<PROJECT_ID>/branches/<BRANCH_ID>`) |
[agent:result] | `postgres_database` | Yes | Postgres database name (default: `databricks_postgres`), not the resource path |
[agent:result] | `create_database_objects_if_missing` | No | Auto-create Postgres schema/database if missing (default: `false`) |
[agent:result] | `new_pipeline_spec.storage_catalog` | Yes | A **regular** UC catalog for DLT pipeline metadata (NOT the Lakebase catalog) |
[agent:result] | `new_pipeline_spec.storage_schema` | Yes | Schema in the storage catalog for pipeline metadata (e.g. `default`) |
[agent:result] | `timeseries_key` | No | Column for deduplication when source has duplicate PKs (latest wins). Performance penalty. |
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] > **Note:** Nulls in PK columns are excluded from sync.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Long-running operation; CLI waits by default. Use `--no-wait` to return immediately.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] **Supported source types:** managed/external Delta tables, managed/external Iceberg tables, views, and materialized views.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] **Check status:**
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ```bash
[agent:result] databricks postgres get-synced-table "synced_tables/<LAKEBASE_CATALOG>.<SCHEMA>.<TABLE>" --profile <PROFILE>
[agent:result] ```
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] **Delete:**
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ```bash
[agent:result] databricks postgres delete-synced-table "synced_tables/<LAKEBASE_CATALOG>.<SCHEMA>.<TABLE>" --profile <PROFILE>
[agent:result] ```
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Deletes the sync pipeline and the UC table entry. The Postgres table remains and must be dropped manually if no longer needed (`DROP TABLE <schema>.<table>`).
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] > **DABs:** The bundle schema includes `synced_database_tables`, but it maps to the Provisioned Terraform resource (`databricks_database_synced_database_table`), not the Autoscaling API. **Do not use `synced_database_tables` in DABs with Autoscaling projects** — it routes through the Provisioned API and may create unintended Provisioned instances. DAB support for Autoscaling synced tables (`postgres_synced_tables`) is blocked on Terraform provider work and not yet available. **For Autoscaling projects, use the CLI commands above.**
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ## Example: Sync NYC Taxi Data to Lakebase
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Sync the `samples.nyctaxi.trips` sample table into Lakebase for low-latency app queries.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] **1. Register a UC catalog** (if not already done — see Prerequisites above).
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] **2. Create the synced table (Snapshot mode):**
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ```bash
[agent:result] databricks postgres create-synced-table <LAKEBASE_CATALOG>.public.nyc_trips \
